#
# A copy from 5.17 into 6.0 (rule syntax: RuleSet). ${source-zone} is the zone given with
# --source-zone; the copy refuses to start without it when one of these columns holds a value.
#
# 5.17 stored these java.util.Date and Timestamp columns as the JVM's local clock time; 6.0
# stores UTC clock time (MOD-I141). A time in the hour the zone repeats when it leaves daylight
# time takes the earlier offset.
transform UP_PORTLET_LIFECYCLE.ENTRY_DATE   local-time-to-utc zone=${source-zone}
transform UP_MUTEX.LOCK_START               local-time-to-utc zone=${source-zone}
transform UP_MUTEX.LOCK_UPDATE              local-time-to-utc zone=${source-zone}
transform UP_MUTEX.LOCK_END                 local-time-to-utc zone=${source-zone}
transform UP_PERSON_DIR.LST_PSWD_CGH_DT     local-time-to-utc zone=${source-zone}
transform UP_PORTLET_LIST.CREATED_ON        local-time-to-utc zone=${source-zone}
transform UP_PORTLET_LIST.UPDATED_ON        local-time-to-utc zone=${source-zone}
